  "vibe": "A dark green #2e3d38 board with a wooden ledge across the bottom, a fat chalk stick and a pink eraser lying on it. Gochi Hand writes the headlines, Neucha reads underneath. The diagrams draw themselves against scene progress rather than the clock — a yellow lens shape strokes on between 5% and 60% of each beat, a pink triangle between 30% and 80% — so every cut looks like a teacher drawing live. A faint wipe smear drifts across the board and chalk dust jitters near the top. Everything sits slightly crooked at 1.2° of rotation, the most in this set, and photos arrive as cream paper sheets pinned to the board. Mechanics: handwriting, drag-to-label, tick-box registers, a roll morph. Best for schools, courses, explainers and community work.",
